 :paras
 ["The decision carries its own conventions. Every opening face is met by its matching closing face, nothing is left open, and the outermost closing carries a gratitude. A person's own words are wrapped in Smile with every word inside left exactly as they wrote it. Four spaces mark each depth of the hierarchy, and every Smile file an instance writes is checked by the living linter of [[t:integrity]]."
 "I asked for it on 1 October 2026. “ensure that all AI prompt writing in the future is only in (: Smile, all markdown, XML etc or other formats are always converted before being run.”, and “You must ensure that all AI text is written in Smile and converted into Smile before anything is run always for all LLMs”. When a conversion came back unconverted, “this appears to still be in markdown. it must be in smile converted”.[[m:2026-10-01]] The same day in osrs, “write everytihng in smile and follow THE MAP, vision documents, decomposition guides”.[[m:2026-10-01#2]] And of how the conversion is written, “inside of the Smile text itself when you decompose his prompt out of markdown and any other format you need tabs or 4 spaces which increase for each hierarchy.”[[m:2026-10-01#3]]"
 "Across {{moments}} moments and {{quotes}} quotes, on {{first}}, the decision arrived in one day. Smile Everywhere carried it into the instructions every instance reads the same day, with the linter hook on every file written after it, while converting everything before a model sees it is still part built. The Markdown it replaces for prompts remains the response format of [[t:semantic-markdown]], and the conversion itself is followed in [[t:sensing-smile-ification]]."],
 :faq
